# location-tracking-system

The location tracking system implements a multi-tiered geolocation service with compliance verification for warrant service areas.

Importance Score: 85/100

Core Components:

1. Provider Fallback Chain (geo.py)
- Primary GPS-based tracking with user consent requirements
- Secondary IP-based geolocation when consent unavailable
- Tertiary cell tower triangulation as final fallback
- Provider-specific response normalization for consistent location data

2. Accuracy Verification
- Radius calculations for location precision assessment
- Minimum accuracy thresholds for warrant service compliance
- Geographic boundary validation for service jurisdictions
- Confidence scoring based on provider source

3. Compliance Monitoring
- VPN/proxy detection to ensure authentic location data
- Jurisdiction validation against authorized service areas
- Consent status tracking and verification
- Location history maintenance for audit purposes

4. Data Flow Model
- Location request initiation via SMS link delivery
- Client-side position capture with accuracy metrics
- Server-side validation and normalization
- Geographic compliance verification
- Location storage with consent status

5. Verification Interfaces (templates/checkin.html, preview.html)
- Consent capture workflow
- Location preview functionality
- Accuracy radius visualization
- Service area boundary display

The system prioritizes accuracy and compliance while maintaining fallback capabilities for scenarios where primary location methods are unavailable.

